  "releaseNotes": "WorkflowForge.Extensions.Logging.Serilog 2.2.0\n\nBREAKING\n- Removed SerilogLoggerFactory.CreateLogger(ILogger). Its parameter was an internalized Serilog type, so the overload could not be called from outside the assembly. Use CreateLogger(SerilogLoggerOptions) or CreateLogger(ILoggerFactory).\n\nFixed\n- Structured properties and scopes reached no sink: the embedded pipeline never enabled Enrich.FromLogContext(), so everything pushed through LogContext was dropped.\n- The logger returned by CreateLogger(SerilogLoggerOptions) now owns and disposes its Serilog pipeline.\n- Dropped the unused Serilog.Extensions.Logging reference, removing a 10.0.10 dependency floor.\n\nFull changelog: https://github.com/animatlabs/workflow-forge/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md#220---2026-09-15",
